<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
	license:CC0-1.0

	Technics SX-WSA1R - ACOUSTIC MODELING SYNTHESIZER MODULE, the 2U rack.

	THE SWITCH MATRIX - where the bindings come from
	================================================
	CP1/CP2 P.C. Diagram, PDF p.32 (manual II-29/30), traced by programmatic
	black-run extraction at 400 dpi: notes/wsa1-probes/wsa1_sch_TRACE.md and the
	three scan scripts beside it.  IC1 = M37471M2196S; SEG0..SEG9 are its scan
	columns (SEG6 pin 40 and SEG10 pin 33 are DEAD STUBS on the rack) and
	SW0..SW7 its return rows.

	Independently, prom_a's own variant-2 switch->LED table at 0xF95088 stores
	0x0000 for a position with no switch.  Relabel its nine rows as the nine
	wired segments and its zero pattern IS the schematic: 58 populated cells =
	47 (CP1) + 11 (CP2), the parts-list counts exactly, with the single hole at
	SEG2/SW7 = SW24/D24 not fitted.  15/15 checks pass in
	notes/wsa1-probes/wsa1_sch_vs_rom_matrix.py.  Nothing from the schematic was
	fed into that script, so it is a genuine second witness to segment<->column,
	bit<->row and population.

	PROVENANCE PER BUTTON.  Every one of the 58 is BOUND, and each carries its
	tier in its own comment:

	  [L]  29 buttons - the schematic PRINTS this legend next to this switch.
	  [B]  19 buttons - net traced, panel position read off the P.C. BOARD page
	                   (PDF p.31), whose orientation is anchored by silkscreen in
	                   BOTH axes (keypad reads 7,8 left-to-right and 7/4/1/0 top-
	                   to-bottom; PAGE is silkscreened up on SW22, down on SW21).
	                   The ROM's family tags corroborate the GROUPING: 0x0608 is
	                   exactly the numeric family (keys 0-9, +/-, ENTER and SEG3
	                   bits 5-7) and 0x0604 exactly the LCD-navigation family.
	  [F]  10 buttons - the ten LCD soft keys.  Their NET is traced like tier B,
	                   but their column was the one reading left resting on the
	                   board page's left-right orientation: neither five-key
	                   column is legended and both carry the ROM family tag
	                   0x0604.  ★ THE FIRMWARE SETTLED IT.  Screen 0x40, the DISK
	                   menu, draws FOUR entries down the left of the LCD (DISK
	                   LOAD / DISK SAVE / MIDI FILE DIRECT PLAY / FLOPPY DISK
	                   FORMAT) and TWO down the right (LOAD SINGLE SOUND / LOAD
	                   SINGLE COMBI.).  Pressing rows 1..5 of each column and
	                   reading the family-B screen the firmware moves to gives

	                     row   SEG9            SEG3
	                      1    47 DISK LOAD    54 LOAD SINGLE SOUND
	                      2    4C DISK SAVE    53 LOAD SINGLE COMBI.
	                      3    45 MIDI FILE    40 no change
	                      4    50 FLOPPY FMT   40 no change
	                      5    40 no change    40 no change

	                   Four live rows on SEG9, two on SEG3 - exactly as the menu
	                   is drawn.  SEG9 IS THE LEFT COLUMN and SEG3 the right.
	                   Reproduce: notes/wsa1-probes/wsa1_softkey_columns.sh

	NOT FITTED, so not drawn and not bound: SEG2/SW7 (SW24), SEG7/SW4..SW7,
	SEG8/SW2..SW7, SEG9/SW5..SW7.  SEG6 and SEG10 exist in the device's port
	list for the SX-WSA1 keyboard only; on this machine segment_is_wired()
	refuses them (wsa1_cpanel.cpp), so nothing here may bind to them.

	THE LAMPS
	=========
	18 lamps on the rack, and prom_a's table names 14 of them outright.  The
	word at 0xF95088 is (LED register << 8) | LED bit mask - confirmed from the
	code, not assumed: sub_F94E1C does `ld WA,(XHL)` and calls 0xF40670 -> the
	UNGUARDED entry of Panel_SetLedRegister (prom_a 0xF8C846), which maps W
	through the register->wire table and queues [wire][A].  So W (the high byte)
	is the register and A (the low byte) is the data.  The driver's output index
	is register*8 + bit, hence the led# numbers below.

	DRAWN BUT NOT BOUND, and why:
	  * the four REALTIME CREATOR ring lamps.  The ROM pins the SET to
	    {led16, led17, led24, led25} (RESET lights reg2 mask 0x03, "1~6" lights
	    reg3 mask 0x03) but not which of the four is north/east/south/west.
	  * the floppy drive's activity lamp - it belongs to the FDD, and the
	    driver exposes no output for it.
	  * CONTRAST.  VR2 on CP2 is an LCD bias pot whose wiper goes back to MAIN
	    as VO; it is not a panel-MCU input and there is no ioport to bind.
	  * POWER, PHONES, the floppy eject button - no port exists for any of them.
	  * REALTIME CREATOR itself is NOT a panel control: it is board MB2's
	    triple-gang VR2, reporting JOYX/JOYY to the MAIN TMP95C061's own A/D
	    (PDF p.19).  Only its four ring lamps are on CP2.  Drawn, inert.

	This layout is for the RACK (wsa1r) only.  The SX-WSA1 keyboard's panel is a
	different board with two extra scan columns and three extra pots, and NO
	document for it exists anywhere, so it deliberately gets no layout rather
	than a silently reused one.
-->
<mamelayout version="2">
	<!-- LN382G / LN282R, unlit fills taken from the artwork (#003000 / #440000). -->
	<element name="led_green" defstate="0">
		<disk state="0"><color red="0.00" green="0.19" blue="0.00"/></disk>
		<disk state="1"><color red="0.15" green="1.00" blue="0.15"/></disk>
	</element>

	<element name="led_red" defstate="0">
		<disk state="0"><color red="0.27" green="0.00" blue="0.00"/></disk>
		<disk state="1"><color red="1.00" green="0.13" blue="0.13"/></disk>
	</element>

